title: Democracy Reforms
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
view-if: voting_policy_timer <= 0 and dem_president = 1 and dem_house = 1 and dem_senate = 1
on-arrival: voting_policy_timer = 10

= Democracy Reforms

The rules of democracy are themselves contested. Reformers want federal standards; skeptics fear overreach.

- @voting_rights_act: Pass voting rights legislation
- @ethics_reform_bill: Ethics and anti-corruption reform
- @fair_maps_bill: Ban partisan gerrymandering
- @filibuster_change: Reform the filibuster
- @easy_discard

@voting_rights_act
on-arrival: voting_rights += 1; election_admin += 6; minority_dem += 3*(1-dissent); polarization += 1; gop_enthusiasm += 0.4; resources -= 0; month_actions += 1

Federal standards protect access to the ballot nationwide.

@ethics_reform_bill
on-arrival: ethics_reform += 1; institutions += 3; pro_democracy += 2; biz_relation -= 2; month_actions += 1

Disclosure rules and conflict-of-interest limits rebuild some public trust.

@fair_maps_bill
on-arrival: gerrymander_bias -= 1.2; institutions += 1; gopmod_relation -= 3; polarization += 0.5; month_actions += 1

Independent commissions draw the lines, nationwide.

@filibuster_change
on-arrival: filibuster_reform += 1; institutions -= 1; progressive_dissent -= 4; moderate_dissent += 4; gopmod_relation -= 6; month_actions += 1

A rules change opens the way for faster legislation, and sharper polarization.
